---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ObfuscatedEmail from '../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Committees" description="The volunteer committees of the Beaumont-Wilshire Neighborhood Association and how to join them.">

  <PageHero
    title="Committees"
    subtitle="Where the work of the association gets done"
    image={`${base}images/hero/hero-movie-blankets`}
    position="center 12%"
  />

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container content-width">

      <h2>Communication</h2>
      <p>
        The Communication Committee ensures that news, events, and activities of interest to
        Beaumont-Wilshire residents are shared clearly and professionally. The group meets
        regularly to coordinate BWNA's communication tools &mdash; the website, the bimonthly
        print newsletter, and the monthly emailed Community Update &mdash; keeping them
        accurate, aligned, and reflective of BWNA's branding standards. Members include the
        newsletter editor, Community Update editor, graphic designer, and the BWNA board
        president.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like to contribute ideas or get involved,
        <a href={`${base}contact`}>contact the Communication Committee Chair</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Crime Prevention &amp; Safety</h2>
      <p>
        This committee helps keep neighbors informed about local crime and safety concerns.
        Members monitor reports of criminal activity and other issues affecting the
        neighborhood, sharing updates with the BWNA board. The committee maintains a positive
        working relationship with our Portland Police Bureau liaison to support timely
        information-sharing and advocacy when needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Interested in joining? Contact Co-chair Patty Nelson at
        <a href="tel:503-281-8035">503-281-8035</a> or Co-chair Bill Markwart at
        <a href="tel:503-282-4610">503-282-4610</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Events</h2>
      <p>
        The Events Committee is where neighbors come together to make community fun happen!
        Meeting monthly, the group brainstorms ideas, then plans and carries out events as BWNA
        resources allow. This energetic team organizes the annual Skidmore Block Party, the
        Art &amp; Garden Tour, Movie in the Park, the neighborhood-wide yard sale, and speaker
        forums.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like to attend a meeting or help out with an event,
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="events@bwnapdx.org" label="email the Events Committee Chair" />.
      </p>

      <h2>Friends of Wilshire Park</h2>
      <p>
        Friends of Wilshire Park (FoWP), operating as a BWNA committee, is a volunteer-driven
        group dedicated to preserving and enhancing Wilshire Park. Working in partnership with
        Portland Parks &amp; Recreation, members help keep the park vibrant, welcoming, and well
        cared for. Their efforts include hosting community events, planting native species,
        fundraising for improvements such as updated playground equipment, and engaging
        neighbors in long-term stewardship of this beloved green space.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to support our neighborhood park?
        <a href={`${base}contact`}>Contact the FoWP Chair</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Land Use</h2>
      <p>
        The Land Use Committee monitors development activity that may affect Beaumont-Wilshire.
        Members track construction notices, zoning changes, and change-of-use permits within the
        neighborhood boundary and may attend public meetings on issues relevant to residents.
        The goal of the committee is to keep the BWNA board informed and prepared to respond to
        land-use matters that shape our community.
      </p>
      <p>
        Interested in participating?
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="root.timothy@gmail.com" label="Contact the Land Use Committee Chair" />.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter Team</h2>
      <p>
        The BWNA newsletter is an all-volunteer effort that has been printed and hand-delivered
        since at least 1988. While its format has evolved over the years, its mission remains the
        same: to provide the most comprehensive source of BWNA board activity and neighborhood
        news to those who live and work in Beaumont-Wilshire.
      </p>
      <p>
        The team meets bimonthly and blends camaraderie with the work at hand. Members include
        the editor, reporters and writers, copy editors, and a graphic designer who prepares the
        layout and ensures all design elements follow BWNA branding standards. Advertising sales
        and service are currently managed by the editor.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're an experienced writer, reporter, or have advertising sales experience &mdash;
        or simply enjoy talking with neighbors about the benefits of advertising in our
        newsletter &mdash; we'd love to have you join us.
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="editor@bwnapdx.org" label="Contact the Newsletter Team Editor" />.
      </p>

      <h2>Plaza</h2>
      <p>
        Working with the Portland Bureau of Transportation (PBOT) and Beaumont Business
        Association in 2026, this committee successfully secured the temporary closure of a
        portion of NE 44th Avenue at Fremont Street to establish
        <a href={`${base}public-plaza`}>Beaumont Crossing</a>, a neighborhood gathering place.
      </p>
      <p>
        A 3-month trial period for the street plaza extends through late September 2026, after
        which its success will be evaluated by PBOT. A positive evaluation could lead to a
        permanent plaza beginning the summer of 2027.
      </p>
      <p>
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="plaza@bwnapdx.org" label="Send questions or comments to the Plaza Committee" />.
      </p>

      <h2>Transportation</h2>
      <p>
        This committee works to identify and advocate for the transportation-related concerns of
        our neighborhood. Pedestrian, cyclist, and driver safety are their priority. The
        committee brings its concerns to the attention of the Portland Bureau of Transportation
        to seek solutions.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're interested in assisting with the important work of this committee,
        <ObfuscatedEmail email="pdx.stmptwn@gmail.com" label="contact the Transportation Committee Chair" />.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
